  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=3t-2,\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1},\\,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $a$ | $-8$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $b$ | $5$ | $10$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$",
  "worked_solution": "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=3(-3)-2=-9-2=-11.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into $y=\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=\\frac{10}{(-2)^{2}+1}=\\frac{10}{5}=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=3(3)-2=9-2=7.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-11+2+7=-2.\n$$",
